# Weatherglass Deep - an island of the library's plan The Gravity Sea (a side island, sunken 20 m, just north of the shoal)
# Weatherglass Shoal's drowned twin: the same weather station on a sandbank that went down on Lift Day - the Stevenson
# screen fallen on its side, the barometer's glass column broken, the station chest in the sand. Three tight reefs,
# kelp; pufferfish. Quest "The Drowned Twin" (5 steps): the drowned station, the drowned log, the pufferfish, the
# drowned chest and the twin's answer.
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe weatherglass_deep) through the editor's own operations. Points (metres over the
# island's own water line; in the world it all lies 20 m lower, under the sea): the station's flat at 2.5 m (r 7 round
# 0 2); the screen at 3 4 (fallen), the barometer at -3 4.
include lib_sea
include lib_gravity
include lib_areas
include lib_features
include lib_highwater
# RESIZE 10-25 (box agent, older-storyline deep pass): Radius 24 -> 58, a side island of Raft's own size class; the
# drowned station stays in the middle.
# DEEP 10-25: the north keeper's drowned house in the north-west (an air pocket, his last note); a reef rock with a cave
# in the south-east (his strongbox); a drowned rowing boat; two buried treasures. Voice: the north keeper Jonas Lund.
new
gen Trees=0 Bushes=0 Rocks=0.3 Harvest=0 BeachThings=0
gen Seed=9741 Radius=58 Height=4 Roughness=0.25 Peaks=1 Shape=0 Style=0 PeakShape=0.3 Cliffs=0.2 BeachWidth=0.1
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.3 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.3 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0.3
generate
elevation -20

# --- Terrain: the station's flat --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
brush flatten at 0 2 r=7 s=20 frames=200 h=2.5
# --- DEEP 10-25 terrain: the keeper's house's floor (north-west), the reef rock's pad (south-east) --------------------
brush flatten at -25 20 r=9 s=20 frames=300 h=2
brush flatten at 30 -25 r=10 s=20 frames=300 h=3
origin
clear at 0 2 r=6
clear at -25 20 r=10
call ar_cave x=30 z=-25 h=3 yaw=0 al=reefrock chest=reefchest

# --- The drowned station: the fallen screen, the broken barometer, the log, the chest ------------------------------
place RT_Pillar - at 2.4 3.4 ground sy=0.35
place RT_Pillar - at 2.4 4.6 ground sy=0.35
place "Box Small" screen at 3.6 4.4 ground sit rot=0,30,85
prop screen tint.color=#9a968a
prop screen tint.amount=0.6
place TP_IcePillar01 barometer at -3 4 ground sit scale=0.35 rot=0,0,70
prop barometer tint.color=#6a8a90
prop barometer tint.amount=0.6
place Note_Sign drownedlog at 0 -2 ground sit rot=6,180,4
place Loot_Chest drownedchest at 1 6.5 ground sit yaw=160
place "Box Small" - at -1.2 6.6 ground sit
place Note_Paper twinanswer at -1.2 6.6 ground y=1.6 drop yaw=20
place Zone_Trigger stationzone at 0 0 ground y=1
place Zone_Trigger pufferzone at 0 2 ground y=2
place Creature_PufferFish puffers at 4 -4 ground y=2

# --- Three tight reefs, kelp ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
scatter VP_CoralBulb04 5 at 10 6 r=3 seed=9751 free=1
scatter VP_CoralFoliose01 4 at 10 6 r=3 seed=9752 free=1
scatter VP_CoralDigitate03 5 at -10 -4 r=3 seed=9753 free=1
scatter TinyCoral 6 at -10 -4 r=3 seed=9754 free=1
scatter VP_CoralBulb06 5 at 2 -12 r=3 seed=9755 free=1
scatter VP_CoralFoliose03 4 at 2 -12 r=3 seed=9756 free=1
scatter SeaVine3 20 at 0 0 r=20 seed=9757 free=2
scatter SeaVine3_klump 6 at 0 0 r=20 seed=9758 free=2
call shallows x=0 z=0 r=66 deep=6 n=2 seed=9759
scatter SeaVine3 30 at 0 0 r=50 seed=9760 free=2
call hw_reef x=35 z=20 r=4 seed=9761
call hw_reef x=-30 z=-30 r=4 seed=9762

# --- DEEP 10-25: the north keeper's drowned house (air), his note, his strongbox in the reef rock, a rowing boat -------
call hw_sunkhouse x=-25 z=20 h=2 yaw=310 a=jonashouse chest=jonaschest air=jonasair bub=jonasbub dal=jonasdoor
call hw_zone x=-25 z=20 al=jonaszone id=jonashouse r=7 h=1 msg="The keeper's house, drowned with its station. The front room still holds air."
place Note_Paper jonasnote at -24 19 h=2.5 drop yaw=310
loot jonaschest CopperOre*2;Battery*1;Rope*2;Cooked_Mackerel*1
prop jonaschest loot.refill=0
note jonaschest Jonas's sea chest | Jonas Lund's sea chest: rope, a battery, a dry fish - and a photograph of two stations on two sandbanks.
call hw_zone x=30 z=-20 al=reefz id=reefcave r=4 msg="A cave in the reef rock. Something wrapped in sailcloth is wedged at the back."
loot reefchest TitaniumOre*1;MetalIngot*1;Bolt*2;Hinge*1
prop reefchest loot.refill=0
note reefchest Keeper's strongbox | The keeper's strongbox, hidden in the reef rock: the station's float money - iron, titanium ore and bolts.
call hw_wreck x=20 z=35 h=2 yaw=200 obj=BoatStranded al=rowboat crate=rowcrate r=7
loot rowcrate Rope*2;Plank*3;Nail*6
note rowcrate Rowing boat's crate | The station's rowing boat, gone down at its mooring: rope, planks, nails.
call treasure x=-35 z=-10 r=4 n=1 seed=9763 kind=0
prop treasure9763 treasure.loot=MetalOre*3;CopperOre*2
call treasure x=10 z=-35 r=4 n=1 seed=9764 kind=0
prop treasure9764 treasure.loot=Scrap*3;Bolt*2;TitaniumOre*1


# --- Settings, notes, behaviours, quest -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Weatherglass Deep
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Weatherglass Shoal's drowned twin, 20 m down: the keeper's drowned house with its air, a reef rock with a cave, a sunken rowing boat, the same weather station gone under on Lift Day, its glass broken, pufferfish in the reef. A side island of The Gravity Sea - dive.
island on.arrive=message||20 m down, in the dark water by the shoal: the same white box on legs - fallen over, in the sand.

note drownedlog Drowned log | WEATHERGLASS TWIN - LOG\n\nLift Day, 3:51. The glass reads 9.9 - off the scale.\n3:52. The bank is sinking. Halvard's lift took the hill; the bill comes here.\n3:53. Going up the boardwalk. Leaving the log.
note drownedchest Drowned chest | The drowned station's chest, sealed with wax: the keeper's valuables.
note jonasnote North keeper Jonas Lund's note | (Written in pencil, on the back of a weather form, the paper dry in the air pocket)\n\nMaja -\n\nThe house went down slower than the station. I had time to shut the door, and the front room kept its air. I have been breathing it for two days. The water outside is very calm and very green.\n\nThe glass read 9.9 at the end. Not the weather - the field. Halvard's lift took the hill up, and the sea took our bank down to pay for it. Up and down, always equal. That is all the glass ever says.\n\nThe station's money is in the reef rock, where the tide could never reach it. Give it to whoever comes down. They will have earned it.\n\n- Jonas
note twinanswer Twin's answer | TO THE SHOAL STATION\n\nIf you are reading this, the field fell, or someone came down anyway. Thank you for coming.\nThe glass told us all along: what goes up must be paid for below.
loot drownedchest TitaniumIngot*1;MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Bolt*2
prop drownedchest loot.refill=0

prop stationzone zone.id=drowned_station
prop stationzone zone.radius=4
prop stationzone zone.message=The drowned station. The barometer's glass lies broken in the sand.
prop pufferzone zone.id=drowned_reef
prop pufferzone zone.radius=10
prop pufferzone zone.repeat=never
prop pufferzone zone.message=Pufferfish swell up round the station!
prop puffers creature.count=3
prop puffers creature.respawn=0
prop puffers creature.zone=drowned_reef

quest title=The Drowned Twin
quest intro=The shoal's twin station lies 20 m down, in the dark water. Dive to it.
step reach|drowned_station|1|Dive down where the sea is darker, to the drowned station
step read|Drowned log|1|Read the drowned station's log
step reach|jonashouse|1|Find the keeper's drowned house, a little way from the station
step read|North keeper Jonas Lund's note|1|Breathe in the house's front room and read the keeper's note
step kill|Puffer fish|3|Drive off the pufferfish
step open|Drowned chest|1|Open the drowned chest
step read|Twin's answer|1|Read the twin's answer
quest done=Both weather stations are read. The glass on the shoal still says: falling toward the dark water.
quest reward=TitaniumIngot*1;MetalIngot*2;Cooked_Mackerel*2

save Weatherglass Deep
